# cahunRules: hunting hours, hunter orange, conveyances, roads and prohibited methods.
# Sources: FWCA ss. 1, 17, 18, 20, 21, 23 to 30; O. Reg. 665/98 ss. 26, 29, 33, 55 to 57,
# 63 to 66, 80, 84, 86, 92; Hunting Regulations Summary 2026 (general regulations, turkey,
# black bear, important messages).
# Stems ask for a fact a trained candidate knows; every option is a lawful-sounding candidate.
SEG = "RUL"
CAT = "cahunRules"
Q = [
('Outside the listed exceptions, how long before sunrise may hunting begin in Ontario?',
 'Half an hour', ['One hour', 'Fifteen minutes', 'Not until sunrise'],
 'Section 20 of the Act bans hunting from half an hour after sunset to half an hour before sunrise, so legal hours run from half an hour before sunrise to half an hour after sunset.'),
('From half an hour after sunset to half an hour before sunrise, how must a firearm be kept in an area usually inhabited by wildlife?',
 'Unloaded and encased', ['Unloaded with the action open', 'Unloaded with a trigger lock', 'Unloaded and carried slung'],
 'Section 20 of the Act requires a firearm in wildlife habitat at night to be unloaded and encased, unless an exception such as night raccoon hunting applies.'),
('For the night firearm rule, on how many sides must a firearm be enclosed to count as encased?',
 'Six', ['Two', 'Four', 'Five'],
 'The Hunting Regulations Summary says that to be encased, a firearm must be enclosed on all six sides, as in a closed gun case.'),
('While hunting raccoon at night with a licensed dog, which firearm is the only one that may be kept loaded and uncased?',
 'A rim-fire rifle', ['A 12-gauge shotgun', 'A centre-fire rifle', 'A crossbow'],
 'Section 80 (4) allows only a rim-fire rifle to be loaded and uncased while hunting raccoon at night, and it must be unloaded and encased in a vehicle or boat.'),
('While hunting raccoon at night with a licensed dog, which use of a light is NOT allowed?',
 'A light shone from a boat', ['A headlamp on the hunter', 'A handheld flashlight', 'A light carried by a partner'],
 'Section 80 (5) bans shining a light that is attached to, or shone from, a vehicle or boat while hunting raccoon at night. A light carried on foot is allowed.'),
('During the spring wild turkey season, what is the latest time a hunter may hunt each day?',
 '7:00 p.m.', ['Noon', 'Sunset', 'Half an hour after sunset'],
 'The summary says spring turkey hunting runs from half an hour before sunrise to 7:00 p.m., an exception to the normal hours.'),
('During which of these open seasons must licensed hunters wear hunter orange?',
 'The open season for bear', ['The spring turkey season', 'A bows-only deer season', 'The fall duck season'],
 'Section 26 requires a hunter orange garment and head cover during the open seasons for deer, elk or moose (other than bows-only seasons) and during the open season for bear, with exemptions.'),
('During a gun season for deer, which of these bird hunters must still wear hunter orange?',
 'A woodcock hunter', ['A duck hunter', 'A Canada goose hunter', 'A cormorant hunter'],
 'Section 26 (3) exempts hunters of double-crested cormorant and migratory game birds, except woodcock. Woodcock hunters must wear orange like everyone else.'),
('What is the minimum area of solid hunter orange the garment must show above the waist?',
 '400 square inches', ['200 square inches', '600 square inches', '1,000 square inches'],
 'Section 26 (2) requires a solid, not open mesh, garment of at least 400 square inches (2,580 square centimetres) above the waist, visible from all sides.'),
("Which of these is allowed under Ontario's hunter orange rules?",
 'A head cover with open mesh', ['A mesh garment above the waist', 'Camouflage orange on the garment', 'A garment of 300 square inches'],
 'The garment must be solid and at least 400 square inches, but the head cover may have open mesh and a brim of another colour. Camouflage orange never counts.'),
('In a bear season with no gun season open for deer, elk or moose, which of these hunters must wear hunter orange?',
 'A bear hunter stalking on foot', ['A bear hunter in a tree stand', 'A grouse hunter', 'An archer in a bows-only deer season'],
 'Section 26 (4) exempts, during the bear season, small game hunters, a bear hunter in a tree stand and hunters in a concurrent bows-only season for deer, elk or moose. A bear hunter on the ground is not exempt.'),
('A friend with no licence and no firearm leads a leashed dog to track a wounded deer with the hunter. Which rule applies to the friend?',
 'Wear hunter orange', ['Carry an Outdoors Card', 'Hold a dog licence', 'Hold a deer licence'],
 'Section 86 (5) lets a tracker follow a wounded animal with a leashed dog without a licence or Outdoors Card if they have no firearm and go with the hunter, and section 86 (6) applies the hunter orange rule to them.'),
('Under section 17 of the Act, in which of these may a deer hunter have a loaded firearm?',
 'A canoe being paddled', ['A motorboat that is drifting', 'A motorboat at anchor', 'A motorboat with its motor raised'],
 'Loaded firearms are banned in or on any conveyance except a boat that is not a motorboat. A motorboat is any boat with a motor attached that can propel it, whether running or not.'),
('For which bird may a hunter shoot from a motorboat that is not moving and has its motor turned off?',
 'Double-crested cormorant', ['Wild turkey', 'Ruffed grouse', 'Sharp-tailed grouse cock'],
 'Section 63.1 lets a cormorant hunter have a loaded firearm in, or shoot from, a motorboat that is not in motion with the motor turned off. Migratory bird hunters follow the federal rules.'),
('Which of these counts as a vehicle under the Act, so a loaded firearm may not be in or on it?',
 'A bicycle', ['A horse', 'A canoe', 'A kayak'],
 'The Act defines a vehicle as anything driven, propelled or drawn on land or ice by any power, including muscular power. A horse is not a vehicle, and paddled boats are exempt boats.'),
('Which of these may NOT be used to find a deer wounded during the hunt?',
 'A drone', ['A dog on a 10 m leash', 'A helper with no firearm', 'A GPS track of the shot'],
 'Section 24 of the Act bans using an aircraft while hunting, and the summary says drones are aircraft, including when searching for a wounded animal.'),
('In parts of Ontario not listed in the road rules, which firearm rule still applies on public roads?',
 'No shooting across the travelled road', ['No loaded firearm on the shoulder', 'No loaded firearm within 8 m', 'No hunting within 400 m of a road'],
 'Section 17 (1) (e) bans discharging a firearm in or across the travelled portion of a public right of way everywhere. The loaded firearm and 8 m rules apply only in the prescribed areas.'),
('In the listed parts of southern Ontario, where there is no fence, how close to the travelled road may a hunter carry a loaded firearm when not on private land?',
 '8 metres', ['3 metres', '15 metres', '30 metres'],
 'Section 65 bans a loaded firearm for hunting on the right of way and, where there is no fence, within 8 metres of the edge of the travelled portion unless the person is on privately owned property.'),
('Which animal does the Act ban using to hunt?',
 'A ferret', ['A falcon', 'A hound', 'A retriever'],
 'Section 28 of the Act bans hunting with a ferret. Falconry and hunting dogs are allowed under their own licences and rules.'),
('Which deer lure is illegal to use or possess in Ontario?',
 'A natural deer urine lure', ['A synthetic deer scent', 'An apple-based attractant', 'A doe bleat call'],
 'Products containing the urine, faeces, blood, gland oil, saliva or other fluids of any cervid are banned to keep out chronic wasting disease. Synthetic and plant-based products are allowed.'),
('Which wild turkey hunting method is legal in Ontario?',
 'A hand-operated box call', ['A live hen decoy', 'An electronic gobble call', 'Hunting 300 m from fresh bait'],
 'Section 33 bans live decoys, electronic calls and hunting within 400 metres of a place where bait has been put unless it has been free of bait for at least 7 days.'),
('Corn was spread in a field for turkeys. How long must the spot be free of bait before turkey may be hunted within 400 metres of it?',
 '7 days', ['2 days', '14 days', '30 days'],
 'Section 33 bans hunting turkey within 400 metres of a place where bait was deposited unless the place has been free of bait for at least seven days.'),
('Which of these is NOT a place where bait has been deposited, for the wild turkey rule?',
 'A field of standing corn', ['Imitation corn kernels', 'Wheat put out near a blind', 'A sack of oats left open'],
 'Section 33 counts grain, other feed and any imitation of feed as bait, but not standing crops, flooded harvested land, properly stacked crops or grain spilled by normal farming.'),
("Without the owner's written permission, how close to a dwelling may bear bait be placed?",
 'No closer than 500 metres', ['No closer than 50 metres', 'No closer than 100 metres', 'No closer than 1 kilometre'],
 'Section 56 bans placing bear bait within 500 metres of a dwelling unless the owner gives written permission, and within 500 metres of a public building.'),
('How close to a public road or a signposted public trail may bear bait be placed?',
 'No closer than 30 metres', ['No closer than 5 metres', 'No closer than 100 metres', 'No closer than 500 metres'],
 'Section 56 bans placing bear bait within 30 metres of a right of way for public vehicular traffic or of an established, signposted recreational trail.'),
('How far from a waste disposal site must a hunter be to hunt bear?',
 'At least 400 metres', ['At least 50 metres', 'At least 200 metres', 'At least 1 kilometre'],
 'Section 57 bans hunting a bear within 400 metres of a waste disposal site, on Crown or private land.'),
('Without a dog licence, how long may the leash be on a dog used to find wounded big game?',
 'No more than 10 metres', ['No more than 3 metres', 'No more than 20 metres', 'No more than 30 metres'],
 "Section 86 (4) allows an unlicensed dog only to search for big game already wounded in the hunt, on a leash no longer than 10 metres and under the handler's physical control."),
('Which big game species may never be hunted with a dog in Ontario?',
 'Elk', ['Black bear', 'White-tailed deer', 'Moose'],
 'Section 86 (2) bans using or being accompanied by a dog when hunting elk. Dogs used to hunt deer, moose or bear must be licensed, and some areas ban them.'),
('South of the French and Mattawa rivers, outside the listed municipalities, which of these may be carried for hunting on a Sunday?',
 'A crossbow', ['A muzzle-loading shotgun', 'A 20-gauge shotgun', 'A rim-fire rifle'],
 'Section 66 bans carrying or discharging any firearm other than a long-bow or crossbow for hunting on a Sunday in that area, except on a licensed game bird hunting preserve.'),
('North of the French and Mattawa rivers, what may a resident small game snare for varying hare be made of?',
 'Brass wire, 22 to 24 gauge', ['Steel wire, 22 to 24 gauge', 'Brass wire, 14 to 16 gauge', 'Braided steel cable'],
 'Section 92 allows only copper or brass wire between 22 and 24 gauge with a loop no more than 10 cm across, for resident small game licence holders north of those rivers.'),
('A small game licence also lets its holder trap which of these animals in a box trap, cage trap or net?',
 'Gray squirrel', ['Raccoon', 'Red fox', 'Striped skunk'],
 'Section 29 lets a small game licence holder trap varying hare, cottontail, European hare, gray squirrel or fox squirrel with a box trap, cage trap or net. Furbearers need a trapping licence.'),
('Which of these may be used to hunt bullfrogs in Ontario?',
 'A long-bow', ['A .22 rim-fire rifle', 'A 20-gauge shotgun', 'An air gun'],
 'Section 84 bans hunting bullfrogs with any firearm other than a long-bow or crossbow. Bullfrogs may also be hunted at night without a firearm, using a light.'),
]
